<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Shiloh cut to underweight.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Shiloh cut to underweight.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald &amp; Co analyst Mark Parr said he cut his rating on Shiloh Industries Inc to underweight from aggressive buy after the company tentatively agreed to be acquired by MTD Products Inc for $19 a share plus assumption of debt.</p>
<p>-- The $19 valuation is in line with his price target, Parr said in a report dated Thursday.</p>
<p>-- On Thursday Shiloh and MTD said certain Shiloh stockholders were in favor of the deal. MTD owns about 36 percent of Shiloh's outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>-- Shiloh shares were off 1-7/8 at 18-3/8.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
